<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28543" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mellīgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			f.
		mel. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A honey-like juice</i>, sucked by the bees from
			flowers, but not yet made into honey, <i>bee-glue,
				bees'rosin, hive-dross</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 6,
				5, § 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 7, 10, §
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The juice of unripe grapes</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uvae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 27, 60, § 131</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
